From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:50:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] FEXCore: validate code in writable pages under mtrack;
 memset call-ret stack on Windows

With SMCChecks=mtrack, blocks whose guest range is writable get per-instruction
code validation, because mixed host-page permissions can hide guest writes from
write-fault tracking. On _WIN32 the call-ret stack is cleared with memset instead
of VirtualDontNeed, which would re-enter guest allocation notifications under the
code lock.

Source: MacRunner lane debug-teb-self-load/writable-validation-clear-fex
(navisworks, 11.09.2026); exact file compiled into MacRunner 1.0.2.

Portions derived from FEX-Emu, Copyright (c) 2019 Ryan Houdek and FEX contributors, MIT License.
Co-Authored-By: GPT-6 Astra <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
index a39c9a130..5ef1a2e61 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@ -637,7 +637,10 @@ ContextImpl::GenerateIR(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, uint64_t Gue
           Thread->OpDispatcher->_GuestOpcode(InstAddress - GuestRIP);
         }
 
-        if (Config.SMCChecks == FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_SMC_FULL || Block.ForceFullSMCDetection) {
+        // Mixed host-page permissions can hide guest writes from write-fault tracking.
+        const bool ValidateWritableCode = Config.SMCChecks == FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_SMC_MTRACK &&
+                                          SyscallHandler->QueryGuestExecutableRange(Thread, InstAddress).Writable;
+        if (Config.SMCChecks == FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_SMC_FULL || Block.ForceFullSMCDetection || ValidateWritableCode) {
           auto ExistingCodePtr = reinterpret_cast<uint8_t*>(Block.Entry + BlockInstructionsLength);
           auto InstAddressReg = Thread->OpDispatcher->_EntrypointOffset(GPRSize, InstAddress - GuestRIP);
           std::array<uint8_t, 0x10> CodeOriginal;
@@ -993,7 +996,12 @@ void ContextImpl::InvalidateThreadCachedCodeRange(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadS
     FEXCORE_PROFILE_SCOPED("InvalidateCallRet");
 
     // This may cause access violations in the thread on Windows as zeroing is not atomic, this is handled by the frontend
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    // This private cache must not re-enter guest allocation notifications under the code lock.
+    memset(Thread->CallRetStackBase, 0, FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState::CALLRET_STACK_SIZE);
+#else
     Allocator::VirtualDontNeed(Thread->CallRetStackBase, FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState::CALLRET_STACK_SIZE);
+#endif
   }
 }
 
